{
  "name": "GenerationJob",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "user_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "user_email": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "job_type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "music",
        "lyrics",
        "cover_art",
        "video",
        "sfx",
        "loop"
      ],
      "description": "Type of generation task"
    },
    "provider": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "loudly",
        "nuro",
        "sonic",
        "producer",
        "tempcolor",
        "ltx",
        "nextcut",
        "shotstack",
        "elevenlabs",
        "harmonix",
        "sirensong",
        "skye",
        "aurora",
        "novah3",
        "soundforge",
        "sever",
        "ondevice",
        "diffsinger",
        "musicgenchord",
        "core",
        "maestro"
      ],
      "description": "Which provider handled the generation. 'nextcut' is retired and kept only for historical rows \u2014 video composition now runs on 'shotstack'. 'core' = the platform's own LLM wrote the lyrics inline. 'sirensong' = Siren Song (HeartMuLa 3B) audio generation on our self-hosted Hugging Face Space engine; the row is created 'processing' at submit and finalized to 'completed' by pollSirenSongJob once the L4 GPU render is fetched and persisted. 'skye' = Skye, our open-source fork of DiffRhythm 2, self-hosted on its own Hugging Face Space; same submit-and-poll lifecycle as sirensong (finalized by pollSkyeJob) but a different model with prose style + negative prompt + optional reference-audio style cloning, and long-form output up to 285s. 'aurora' = Aurora, our own self-hosted deployment of the open-weight MiniMax-Music3 model (MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-Music3), finalized by pollAuroraJob. Deliberately DISTINCT from 'tempcolor' even when Tempolor is routing a MiniMax family model: that is a third-party hosted service on its own contract, pricing and output format, while an aurora row attests to weights we run ourselves \u2014 collapsing the two would leave a provenance record unable to say which one produced the track. Aurora rows carry the model's structured caption (or the creator's prose) plus the section-tagged lyrics, render complete songs up to 300s, and output native 32kHz 16-bit stereo PCM, so they are the only prompt-generated rows guaranteed lossless at source. The row also records the MiniMax-Music3 attribution required by that model's community licence. 'novah3' = Nova, our own self-hosted deployment of the open-weight MiniMax-H3 omni model (MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3) on a ZeroGPU worker, finalized by pollNovaH3Job. Video work, deliberately NOT filed under 'ltx': LTX is a third-party per-second cloud API with its own model ladder, while a novah3 row attests to weights we run ourselves, and the two cannot be told apart after the fact if they share a provider value. A novah3 row is also the only video row whose SOUNDTRACK was generated jointly with the picture in one denoising pass rather than dubbed on afterwards \u2014 input_data records the canvas label, the snapped frame count, the step preset and any keyframe/omni references, because H3's VAE snaps length to 17n+5 frames and the delivered duration is therefore never exactly the one requested. Carries the MiniMax-H3 attribution its community licence requires. 'sever' = Sever, our self-hosted HTDemucs-6s stem separation engine; it REPLACES 'tempcolor' for separation, so a tempcolor separation row is historical. Sever rows are separation work, never generation \u2014 the stems inherit the source's GenAI label rather than being labelled as newly generated audio. 'ondevice' = the SAME htdemucs_6s model run locally in the creator's own browser via onnxruntime-web; recorded as its own provider rather than as 'sever' because no audio ever reached our engine, which is exactly the fact a provenance record must not blur. An ondevice row is never billed. 'diffsinger' = Cantor, our self-hosted DiffSinger singing-voice engine; it renders a HUMAN-AUTHORED LeadSheet melody, so a diffsinger row is the only generation path whose vocal line is composed rather than prompted \u2014 its rows carry ai_label 'ai_assisted' rather than 'ai_generated', and input_data always names the lead_sheet_id and score_hash the render came from. Finalized by pollDiffSingerVocals. 'musicgenchord' = Cadence, our self-hosted MusicGen-Chord engine (multi-hot chord chroma over stock musicgen-melody weights), rendering an instrumental bed from a LeadSheet's LITERAL chord progression rather than from a prose prompt. The name is kept model-shaped rather than engine-shaped because the conditioning method, not the host, is what the row attests to \u2014 it was briefly served from Replicate before the engine was brought in-house, and those historical rows describe the same conditioning. Like diffsinger these rows are 'ai_assisted' because the harmony is authored, but their participation score is deliberately lower \u2014 the progression is human while the arrangement and instrumentation are generated, and conflating the two would overstate authorship. Finalized by pollMusicGenChordBed. 'maestro' = the row is a WORK ORDER for the Maestro Superagent's craft engine: it is created 'pending' with nothing generated yet, and the Maestro sweep is what fills output_metadata and flips it to 'completed'. Nothing else may complete a maestro row, otherwise the craft engine would be silently bypassed."
    },
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "pending",
        "processing",
        "completed",
        "failed",
        "cancelled"
      ],
      "default": "pending"
    },
    "ai_label": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "ai_generated",
        "ai_assisted",
        "human"
      ],
      "description": "RIAA/IFPI GenAI track-level label (July 2026 standard). ai_generated = GenAI created the entirety/primary portion of the sound recording; ai_assisted = substantially human recording with some GenAI expressive elements; human = no GenAI in the recording. Applies to sound recordings only (not lyrics/cover art/video)."
    },
    "input_data": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Generation parameters (mood, genre, duration, etc.). For a maestro lyrics work order this is the full brief the craft engine reads: topic, genre, mood, bpm, duration, title and the draft sound_prompt. For a diffsinger or musicgenchord row it carries lead_sheet_id and score_hash \u2014 the render is only attributable because those are recorded at submit time. A musicgenchord row also stores BOTH the writer's own chord notation and the normalized Harte form actually sent to the engine, so a render stays reproducible even if the normalizer is later improved. For an aurora row it carries caption_mode ('structured' or 'prose') and, when structured, the individual caption_fields the creator filled in \u2014 a structured caption and a free paragraph are different authorship inputs, and the COS engine reads the difference rather than inferring it. For a novah3 row it carries the canvas label, requested and snapped duration, frame count, step preset and the reference URLs (keyframes or omni references), because H3's own VAE decides the final length and a reproducible render needs the values the engine actually received."
    },
    "output_url": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "URL to generated file"
    },
    "output_metadata": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "BPM, key, duration, etc. For a completed maestro lyrics job this carries the mastercraft results the music job is then built from: 'lyrics' (the enhanced lyric) and 'sound_prompt' (the production-optimized style brief)."
    },
    "credits_used": {
      "type": "number",
      "default": 0
    },
    "error_message": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "provider_job_id": {
      "type": "string"
    },
    "started_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "completed_at": {
      "type": "string",
      "format": "date-time"
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "maxLength": 1000,
      "description": "Optional description for SEO and discoverability"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "user_id",
    "job_type",
    "provider"
  ],
  "rls": {
    "create": {
      "data.user_id": "{{user.id}}"
    },
    "read": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.user_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "update": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.user_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "delete": {
      "$or": [
        {
          "data.user_id": "{{user.id}}"
        },
        {
          "user_condition": {
            "role": "admin"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}